ok   the line: UTC time with milliseconds, the level in capitals, the message, every level
ok   real time has milliseconds and follows travel_back
ok   a travel without a block, freeze_time and travel_back move the line's time
ok   Logger.timestamp formats the followed instant; -1 is real time
ok   a level below the logger's is silent; a message ending in a newline gets no second one
ok   JSON lines: time, level, tags, message
ok   format_line puts the request id apart from the other tags in JSON, in place in text
ok   a JSON line's message drops the line's own newline
ok   the byte scan refuses what is not UTF-8: every byte from 0x80 up is replaced
ok   valid UTF-8 is kept: U+10FFFF, U+2028, a CJK character, an emoji
ok   messages with control bytes, invalid UTF-8 and non-ASCII are one valid JSON line
ok   a JSON line's tag holding invalid UTF-8 or a newline stays one valid JSON line
ok   a long text line is one line, whole
ok   a text message with LF, CR and CRLF is one line, each written as backslash-n or backslash-r
ok   a text message's own last line feed ends the line; any other is escaped
ok   a tag with a line feed or a carriage return stays inside its brackets on one line
ok   nothing else is escaped: a backslash, a tab, other control bytes and non-UTF-8 bytes stay as they are
ok   a text message without a line feed or a carriage return is written byte for byte as before
ok   a forged line in a text message stays inside the one line
ok   JSON lines do not change: a newline in the message or a tag is JSON's own escape
ok   capture_log answers what Cybertrain.logger wrote, debug included, and puts the logger back
